# What a build never needs, and what must never reach an image layer.
**/target
.git
.github
.env*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
compose.pinned.yaml

# A build reads its Dockerfile and this file from disk, not from what is
# copied in. Left out of that, an edit to either does not make every image
# compile again.
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# The images are compiled by the toolchain their base image holds, which the
# Dockerfiles name by digest. With this file in the build, rustup reads it,
# finds the channel's newest patch release is not the one installed, and
# downloads that one in the middle of the build: the compiler would then be
# whatever was newest that day, not the one the digest names.
rust-toolchain.toml
